Index: openwiki/.claims/cell-lifecycle.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/cell-lifecycle.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/cell-lifecycle.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,128 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:2376dbed6b28fe78b61bef4f9dbe5fc2ea89cc3e679385667d7472de8fb24914",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8ca7835443174bea81c9b332396df2a4",
+      "statement": "celld's Phase state machine maps Durable Object lifecycle states onto explicit phases: Resident is active/idle, Dormant is out of memory but still owned (hibernated if sockets survived), Inactive is owned by nobody and is every cell's initial state.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L110-L201",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d7a65f982914195b66941024782ef569bef621dae1caeb10144b535539d36437:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3c19f247ec624b9692148de7f9562bbf",
+      "statement": "evict means different things in celld vs Cloudflare: celld evicts a cell out of memory (Dormant) while Cloudflare evicts it off the host (Inactive), and shedding is what publishes a celld cell unowned.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L110-L117",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ec659a229baa266c5d2accf10d866fa24ee49831ee1eb89468aa81c1f0742fca:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_541ffd87b7cb42dc8c3e7a20251391d1",
+      "statement": "Cold activation of an inactive cell reads owner/lease state, recovers any unsealed dead owner's node log (takeover interlock) before claiming, performs an owner-record CAS bounded by MAX_ACQUIRE_RECONCILES=3 ambiguous-CAS re-reads, then restores SQLite and starts the runtime.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L104-L110",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d5f9370fb17f91fbba71026b6e707f93d566ec5e0ba5e83b4833abc0822a0745:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L769-L792",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5c42ce20f84bed8d27fff7ff3a673931545382575e935483357d30051eb40cfb:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_53902dbff55844f8ad9dc04cfe7f7751",
+      "statement": "Activation restores the cell's SQLite from the newest safe source chosen by a pure sans-IO durability predicate among local eviction snapshot and replicated bucket; availability checks are the executor's IO.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/restore.rs#L5-L13",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0138d5b8cdade0e1a9af345c544f325f37df7c433aaa4863515197cf9b7f15bd:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_2f44f1a211354f4b94e66344fc3004e3",
+      "statement": "Alarm retry policy is a pure function of a persisted retry row: 2-second exponential backoff capped at shift 6, alarm abandoned after 6 limit-counting failures; excused failures like pressure sheds back off but never count toward the ceiling.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/alarm.rs#L4-L19",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4f2116f4e3e40d0a12b39ae3728d345cfcc4eea99733eb6d85b91bb20cd3d571:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f011e96db4894e6fbcd45015674eba0a",
+      "statement": "Wake entry reconciliation is a pure WakeCore::decide transition with executor ordering rules, so production's async bucket flusher and any deterministic fake obey one rule set; the wake index keys on minute buckets.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/wake.rs#L5-L9",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:260090e1c09e21d198a730f2172de41b58eb17c05a5c8456c8ba5ce4f8167e6a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0258858e018f4ccea2264ee9d732c429",
+      "statement": "A wrangler triggers.crons entry becomes one reserved cell whose alarm is armed at the next occurrence; cron resolution is one minute in UTC, matching Cloudflare cron triggers and the wake minute buckets.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/cron.rs#L7-L17",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:047e8f86c2b1ca68c2040f703308f52212cf7a958a47b09ffa53d6ee3969240a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0ae4de013c534f9c9580f3e3b2ef7252",
+      "statement": "A queue is one reserved cell: the cell owns SQL and dispatch, while logic::queue owns stable address, bounds, alarm deadline, admission, retry timing, lease-generation advancement, settlement fencing and purges; PlannedLease carries the generation so callers cannot skip advancing it.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/queue.rs#L3-L11",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b0a097bf229c2d91cd3645d7d646a05b1c40218d33a05791bc89d0b91df4daf8:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_6520bc47532b4bdba60662a988b7496c",
+      "statement": "Cell sweeps are bounded per turn (256 rows) and share one harness between KV and Queues so no cell-backed feature can silently run an unbounded cleanup loop.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/sweep.rs#L4-L10",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2715fed50dca1d6492ba996d99561672cdf260eebb06a132d4d9889399061a79:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a1ef0f0c92f84702916870c0b32ddf84",
+      "statement": "Cell scopes are a security fence: valid_cell_scope allows only ASCII alphanumerics plus _ - . : $ up to 255 bytes and rejects dot-dot names so a scope always forms exactly one filesystem/bucket path component.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/cell.rs#L1-L51",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ea9d8ae877d4427ad45106db82528a333ad481169952f39b6a361e05223df445:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_910949fa4731433eaa15ae6da60dc0d5",
+      "statement": "Regular and outbound WebSockets pin their cell's resident runtime so events still run locally after quiescing starts, while hibernatable sockets survive idling; outbound socket creation is budgeted.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L391-L400",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d453bdc615e6ccd17b90f31abf0396383e545247a2ba172c62a210617109479:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L471-L481",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28e1038c68aa10049147ba58ca253cbb5f4810cd83e3712737742ab05c83abf8:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-11T15:23:20.669Z"
+  }
+}

